---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'How to Book and Ride China High-Speed Rail: Step-by-Step Guide';
const description = 'Book high-speed train tickets in China with just your passport — Trip.com or the official 12306 English site. Step-by-step booking, station, and onboard guide.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/en/transport/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Transport
      </a>
    </nav>
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🚄 Trains</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        How to Book and Ride China High-Speed Rail
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Book tickets with nothing but your passport, find your way through the station, and ride China's fastest trains — step by step.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: August 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 8 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
        You can ride China's high-speed trains on <strong>nothing but your passport</strong> — no Chinese ID card, no Chinese phone number, no local bank account. Two ways to buy: <a href="https://www.trip.com/t/nUumZWrKUV2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-700 underline font-semibold">Trip.com</a> (pays with Visa or Mastercard, no 12306 account needed) or the official <strong>12306 English site</strong>, where foreign passports have been verifiable online since late 2023. Arrive 30–40 minutes early. Your passport <em>is</em> your ticket: you'll show it at security, at the boarding gate, and sometimes again onboard.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#booking" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎫 Booking Your Ticket</a></li>
        <li><a href="#passport" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🛂 Buying on 12306 with a Passport</a></li>
        <li><a href="#station" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚉 At the Station</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">✏️ Changing or Canceling</a></li>
        <li><a href="#bring" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🧳 What You Can and Cannot Bring</a></li>
        <li><a href="#onboard" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚄 On the Train</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">

      <h2 id="booking" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🎫</span> How to Book Your Ticket
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">Three options, from easiest to most involved:</p>

      <ol class="space-y-3 mb-12 list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Trip.com (recommended for most travelers)</strong> — no booking fee, pulls real-time availability straight from the 12306 system, and needs no separate 12306 account. You book with your passport number and board with the same passport. Pays with Visa, Mastercard, or Apple Pay.</li>
        <li><strong>12306 (official — English site/app)</strong> — China Railway's own sales channel. Prices are identical to Trip.com; the difference is you buy direct from the operator, with no booking fee and no middleman holding your order. Foreigners register with a passport, clear a one-time identity check, then book as usual. Payment: international bank cards, plus Alipay or WeChat Pay if you have them set up. Full walk-through in the next section.</li>
        <li><strong>Station ticket counter</strong> — walk up to any station, tell the staff your destination and departure time, and bring your <em>physical</em> passport (a photo will not work). Prices are identical to online. English is not guaranteed at every counter, though the busiest stations (Beijing South, Shanghai Hongqiao, Guangzhou South) almost always have someone who speaks English.</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mb-12">
        <a href="https://www.trip.com/t/nUumZWrKUV2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-xl font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition no-underline text-base">
          👉 Book train tickets on Trip.com →
        </a>
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 id="passport" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🛂</span> Buying on 12306 with a Passport — Step by Step
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">Until late 2023, a foreign passport holder who wanted to buy on 12306 basically had to visit a station counter to get verified first. China Railway changed that: passports can now be checked online, inside the app or website. That single change is what makes booking direct realistic for a short trip.</p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">The English site (<a href="https://www.12306.cn/en/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">12306.cn/en</a>) is a separate front end built for foreign travelers — it accepts <strong>only foreign passports</strong>, so you'll never be asked for a Chinese ID number.</p>

      <div class="my-10 not-prose">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 680 200" class="w-full h-auto" role="img" aria-label="Passport booking flow: Register, Add passenger, Verify identity, Book and pay, Board with passport">
          <defs>
            <marker id="hsrArrow" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#3b82f6"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <!-- connectors -->
          <line x1="128" y1="70" x2="144" y2="70" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#hsrArrow)"/>
          <line x1="264" y1="70" x2="280" y2="70" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#hsrArrow)"/>
          <line x1="400" y1="70" x2="416" y2="70" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#hsrArrow)"/>
          <line x1="536" y1="70" x2="552" y2="70" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#hsrArrow)"/>
          <!-- node 1 -->
          <rect x="10" y="40" width="118" height="120" rx="14" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="69" cy="70" r="16" fill="#3b82f6"/>
          <text x="69" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff">1</text>
          <text x="69" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e3a8a">Register</text>
          <text x="69" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">12306.cn/en</text>
          <text x="69" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">or the app</text>
          <!-- node 2 -->
          <rect x="146" y="40" width="118" height="120" rx="14" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="205" cy="70" r="16" fill="#3b82f6"/>
          <text x="205" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff">2</text>
          <text x="205" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e3a8a">Add passenger</text>
          <text x="205" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">Name +</text>
          <text x="205" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">passport no.</text>
          <!-- node 3 -->
          <rect x="282" y="40" width="118" height="120" rx="14" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="341" cy="70" r="16" fill="#3b82f6"/>
          <text x="341" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff">3</text>
          <text x="341" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e3a8a">Verify ID</text>
          <text x="341" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">Auto, upload</text>
          <text x="341" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">or counter</text>
          <!-- node 4 -->
          <rect x="418" y="40" width="118" height="120" rx="14" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="477" cy="70" r="16" fill="#3b82f6"/>
          <text x="477" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff">4</text>
          <text x="477" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e3a8a">Book &amp; pay</text>
          <text x="477" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">Pick train,</text>
          <text x="477" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">pay by card</text>
          <!-- node 5 -->
          <rect x="554" y="40" width="118" height="120" rx="14" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="613" cy="70" r="16" fill="#3b82f6"/>
          <text x="613" y="75" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff">5</text>
          <text x="613" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e3a8a">Board</text>
          <text x="613" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">Show</text>
          <text x="613" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">passport</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-3 text-center">Your passport is the only ID you need — from creating the account to walking onto the platform.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">The five steps:</p>

      <div class="space-y-8 mb-12">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">1️⃣ Register</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Go to <a href="https://www.12306.cn/en/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">12306.cn/en</a> or download the 12306 app and switch the language to English. Sign up with an email address. During registration you can scan your passport to auto-fill your information, which is much more convenient. We recommend the app.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">2️⃣ Add yourself as a passenger</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Open "My Passengers" and enter your name and passport number. This is the step where most verifications fail — read the name rule below before you type anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">3️⃣ Verify your identity</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The system tries an automatic check first. If it can't confirm you, upload a photo of your passport information page for manual review — this usually comes back within a day or two. If online review still doesn't clear, walk into any station ticket window with your physical passport; staff verify you on the spot in a couple of minutes.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">4️⃣ Search, book, pay</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Once your passenger status reads "verified," pick your date, train, and seat class, then pay by international card. Add travel companions the same way — each needs their own passport details and their own verification.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">5️⃣ Board with your passport</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">There's no paper ticket to collect. Use the farthest-right lane for manual inspection, hand your passport to the staff member (the automated gates only read Chinese ID cards), and go find your carriage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📝 The name rule that decides whether verification works</h3>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Enter the name <strong>exactly</strong> as printed on the passport's machine-readable info page:</p>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm mb-8 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left">
          <thead class="bg-gray-900 text-white">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Do</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Don't</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 text-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Latin letters only (A–Z)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Chinese characters, accents, or non-Latin scripts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Surname first, then given names, in passport order</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Reordering to "given name first" because it looks natural</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">One single space between name parts</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Extra spaces, hyphens you added yourself, or commas</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">The full name as printed</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top">Titles like Mr / Mrs / Miss / Dr. — these are not needed</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">If the printed name runs longer than the field allows (64 characters), enter as much as fits from the start. A mismatch of even one character is the usual reason an automatic check bounces.</p>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-900 font-bold mb-3">🔑 Two rules that surprise people</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
          <li><strong>Real-name ticketing:</strong> Each person may purchase only one ticket per time slot. For example, if you hold a ticket for 10:00–12:00 on a given day, any attempt to buy another for 11:00–13:00 will fail.</li>
          <li><strong>It's an e-ticket:</strong> your passport <em>is</em> the ticket. You can print an itinerary slip at a station machine for your expense report, but that slip is <strong>not</strong> valid for boarding — bring the passport.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 id="station" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🚉</span> At the Station — Step-by-Step
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">Arrive 30–40 minutes before departure. Here is what happens, in order:</p>

      <div class="space-y-8 mb-12">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🛂 Security check</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Every bag goes through an X-ray machine. Similar to airport security but faster; you do not need to take out liquids, laptops, or power banks. Takes about 2–3 minutes unless the station is unusually busy.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">📺 Waiting hall</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Find your gate number on the big departure screen. All major stations show gate numbers in both Chinese and English, plus train status ("On time", "Boarding", "Arrived").</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🎫 Ticket gate</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The regular automated gates read Chinese ID cards only. As a foreign passport holder, look for the manual counter lane, usually at the far left or far right of the gate bank, marked "人工通道" (manual passage). Checking starts about 15 minutes before departure. Hand your passport to the staff; they scan it and wave you through in about 10 seconds.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚃 Find your carriage</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">On the platform, look for colored floor markers. Each carriage number has a colored dot; a large screen by the staircase shows the color code for your train. Match the color to the floor marker so you know where to stand, since trains stop with specific doors at specific positions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Your passport is your ticket.</strong> Keep it in your hand from the moment you enter the station until you sit down. You'll show it at least twice — at security and at the boarding gate. On some routes, staff walk through the carriage after departure for a random passport check.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 id="changes" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">✏️</span> Changing or Canceling Your Ticket
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">The rules are the same whether you booked on Trip.com or 12306:</p>

      <ul class="space-y-3 mb-12 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Change (改签):</strong> Move to a different train on the same day — free if done more than 48 hours ahead. Switching to a later date costs 5%–40%, depending on how close the new date is to the original. Do it through the 12306 English site/app or any station counter.</li>
        <li><strong>Refund:</strong> Same channels. Free more than 8 days before departure; 5% from 48 h–8 days; 10% from 24–48 h; 20% within 24 h.</li>
        <li><strong>No-show:</strong> Miss the train without changing or canceling in time, and you forfeit the full ticket value. There is no grace period.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 id="bring" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🧳</span> What You Can and Cannot Bring
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">These rules are based on the <em>Railway Passenger Prohibited &amp; Restricted Items Directory</em> (《铁路旅客禁止、限制携带和托运物品目录》), the official regulation published by China Railway.</p>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm mb-8 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left">
          <thead class="bg-gray-900 text-white">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Item</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Limit</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 text-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Power bank</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">≤ 100Wh (≈ 27,000 mAh)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Capacity must be clearly marked on the casing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Perfume / cosmetic sprays</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Single container ≤ 100ml</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Non-pressurized, non-flammable types</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Aerosols (hairspray, sunscreen)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">≤ 150ml each, ≤ 600ml total</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Standard travel-size cans</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Nail polish / remover</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">≤ 50 ml total</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Pack only what you need</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Lighter</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">≤ 2</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Standard disposable lighters</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Alcohol (sealed factory bottles)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">≤ 3,000 ml, 24%–70% ABV</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Factory-sealed with a clear label; no refills</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Small tools (scissors, fruit knife)</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Blade &lt; 60mm</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Blade 60mm or longer cannot be brought on at all</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top font-medium">Fishing rod, tripod, umbrella</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Extended ≤ 130cm</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 align-top text-sm">Collapse and pack properly on bullet trains</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-6">Items you cannot bring on the train at all:</p>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-12">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Guns, ammunition, and explosives</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Of any kind — no exceptions.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Flammable liquids</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Gasoline, kerosene, and alcohol over 70% ABV.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Self-heating food</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Self-heating hot pot, self-heating rice — the steam can set off smoke detectors on high-speed trains. This catches more foreign tourists than anything else; if found, it may be confiscated.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Hydrogen-filled balloons</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Not allowed onboard or inside stations.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Corrosives, radioactive materials, and poisons</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Includes strong acids, alkalis, bleach in large quantities, and any toxic substance.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Restricted knives with locking mechanism</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Blade 60mm or longer that have a locking mechanism.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Long blades 60mm or longer</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Kitchen knives, utility knives, machetes — cannot be brought on at all (shorter blades &lt; 60mm are allowed in carry-on).</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Blunt weapons</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Baseball bats, hammers, heavy tools, and anything that could be used as a weapon.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚫 Bicycles and e-scooters</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Unless fully disassembled and packed inside rigid luggage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 id="onboard" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🚄</span> On the Train — What to Expect
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-8 mb-12">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">💺 Seats</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Second class is a 3+2 layout, similar to airline premium economy — fine for most people up to about 185cm. First class is 2+2 with wider seats and more legroom, worth it on journeys over 3 hours. Business class is 2+1 with fully reclining seats.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🔌 Power outlets</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Most G-series trains (300–350 km/h) have two-prong Chinese sockets under the seats. Some older D-series trains (200–250 km/h) may lack outlets at every seat — bring a <a href="/en/life/packing-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">power bank as backup</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🍜 Food and drink</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">A trolley comes through once or twice, selling boxed meals (about ¥40 / $5.50), snacks, instant noodles, and drinks. The coffee is instant. Longer routes have a dining car with a slightly better selection.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🚻 Restrooms</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">At both ends of each carriage. Cleanliness varies by route and time of day; the one at the start of the journey is usually clean, less so by midpoint. Bring your own hand sanitizer and toilet paper.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">📢 Announcements</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Station names in Chinese and English. Displays above the doors show the next stop, current speed, and outside temperature. The English audio is sometimes hard to parse, so watch the display too.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🌡️ Temperature</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">A/C runs around 22–24°C year-round. Even in July, a light jacket or long sleeve is advisable.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">🧳 Luggage storage</h4>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Overhead racks fit carry-on-sized bags. Large suitcases (24"+) go in the rack at the end of each carriage or under the seat. Keep an eye on end-of-carriage bags at intermediate stops.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

